// Default markdownlint rules for repos that do not ship their own config.
//
// markdownlint-cli2 does NOT look above the current directory and ignores any config in your
// home directory, so this file only takes effect when something passes it with --config.
// That is what bin/md-lint does.
//
// A repo that disagrees wins: drop a .markdownlint-cli2.jsonc in it and md-lint steps aside.
//
// This is an allowlist, not the stock ruleset minus exceptions. The stock ruleset reports 654
// issues across 55 files in this repo alone - mostly agent prompts and skill docs written by
// other tools - and a linter that is always wrong gets ignored, which is how ai/CLAUDE.md's
// markdown rules ended up unenforced in the first place. So: "default": false, and then only
// the rules ai/CLAUDE.md actually asks for. Adding a rule here is a deliberate act.
//
// Do NOT add a "globs" key. markdownlint-cli2 appends config globs to the command line, so a
// glob here makes `md-lint README.md` lint the whole tree.
{
  "config": {
    "default": false,

    // "Consistent heading levels"
    "MD001": true,

    // "blank lines around headings and code blocks"
    "MD022": true,
    "MD031": true,

    // "one list marker style" - dash, because that is what this repo already uses
    "MD004": { "style": "dash" },

    // "no trailing whitespace"
    "MD009": true

    // Deliberately absent: MD013 (line length) contradicts "never hard-wrap lines"; MD033
    // (inline HTML) fires on the HTML comments several docs here use for scaffolding notes;
    // MD060 (table column style) fires on every compact table in the repo.
  },
  "ignores": ["**/node_modules/**", "**/.git/**"]
}
